From: hamza <hamza@book4>
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] ufs: qcom: avoid repeated lane clock enables

ufs_qcom_setup_clocks() enables the lane clocks while bringing a link out
of Hibern8, and ufs_qcom_resume() enables them again before the link state
changes. The HCE enable notification also uses the same helper.

The disable helper already uses is_lane_clks_enabled to release the clocks
only once, but the enable helper takes a fresh reference on every call.
Repeated resume cycles therefore leak clock references. In this tree the
bulk list includes all controller clocks, including the reference clock.
On the Book4 these counts grow into the hundreds and the reference-clock
RPMh request remains enabled after device suspension.

Make the enable helper idempotent, matching its disable counterpart.
Keep the flag clear on enable failure so a later call can retry.

The extracted helpers fail the clock-reference regression check before
this change and pass afterward. The corrected module has booted, and a
suspend-callback diagnostic verifies that its reference-clock sleep request
clears. Power savings remain unmeasured.
---
 drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -356,6 +356,9 @@ static int ufs_qcom_enable_lane_clks(struct ufs_qcom_host *host)
 {
 	int err;
 
+	if (host->is_lane_clks_enabled)
+		return 0;
+
 	err = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(host->num_clks, host->clks);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
